<article class="env-lemma" id="0D4I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D4I">Lemma <span data-tag="0D4I">37.30.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of schemes. Let $n_{X/Y}$ be the function on $Y$ giving the dimension of fibres of $f$ introduced in Lemma <a href="/tag/05F8" data-tag="05F8">37.30.2</a>. Then $n_{X/Y}$ is upper semi-continuous. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Z_ d = \{ x \in X \mid \dim _ x(X_{f(x)}) > d\} $. Then $Z_ d$ is a closed subset of $X$ by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FZ" data-tag="02FZ">29.29.4</a>. Since $f$ is proper $f(Z_ d)$ is closed. Since $y \in f(Z_ d) \Leftrightarrow n_{X/Y}(y) > d$ we see that the lemma is true. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>